{"name":"Maud","hex":"#988286","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Maud","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from the Germanic languages.","A village in Aberdeenshire council area, Scotland ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Maud"}],"entries":[{"title":"Queen Maud Land","blocks":[{"text":"Queen Maud Land is a roughly 2.7-million-square-kilometre (1.0-million-square-mile) region of Antarctica claimed by Norway as a dependent territory. It borders the claimed British Antarctic Territory 20° west, specifically the Caird Coast, Coats Land on the West, and the Australian Antarctic Territory 45° east, specifically Enderby Land on the East. In addition, a small unclaimed area from 1939 was annexed in June 2015. Positioned in East Antarctica, it makes out about one-fifth of the continent, and is named after the Norwegian Queen Maud (1869–1938)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Antarctica%2C_Norway_territorial_claim_%28Queen_Maud_Land%2C_2015%29.svg/330px-Antarctica%2C_Norway_territorial_claim_%28Queen_Maud_Land%2C_2015%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queen_Maud_Land","wikidata":"Q189999"},{"title":"Queen Maud Gulf","blocks":[{"text":"Queen Maud Gulf lies between the northern coast of the mainland and the southeastern corner of Victoria Island in Nunavut, Canada. At its western end lies Cambridge Bay, leading to Dease Strait; to the east lies Simpson Strait; and to the north, Victoria Strait. It is home to the Queen Maud Gulf Migratory Bird Sanctuary."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Map_indicating_Queen_Maud_Gulf%2C_Nunavut%2C_Canada.png/330px-Map_indicating_Queen_Maud_Gulf%2C_Nunavut%2C_Canada.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queen_Maud_Gulf","wikidata":"Q2122604"}],"im